  "body": "Stacked on #2968. Review the [changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/1962fd5dc...issue/2957-agie-die-opening).\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR adds a die opening to the native wire EDM job files post. It is ported onto the zero-step setup of #2984, the measured heights of #2964 and the reentrant checks of #2968. The old branch wrote its own SBL through `jescript.rs`. That writer is deleted on main, and this port does not use it.\n\n- **Selection (app).** A Wire Contour with `side: die` takes the edge chains of the upper rim of one through-opening in one retained plate. CamCraft compares the picked rim with the full-height opening of the closed vertical prism. An outer rim, an incomplete rim and a blind floor are refused (`crates/app/src/operation/agie_profile.rs`).\n- **Die setup (post).** `PunchSetup20::encode_die` writes the zero-step setup of `encode` with one changed field: `ID_PUNCH,c_die`. It refuses every thickness other than 20 mm (`SetupError::UnqualifiedDieHeight`). The controller review adds a check of the c_die side, the inward offsets and the slug support. The punch output does not change.\n- **Mirrored geometry (post).** A die opening must be convex. The post reverses it to clockwise, so the retained plate is on the left and the waste on the right, as for a punch. The envelope check (renamed `check_cut_envelope`) then offsets toward the waste inside the opening. Its `cross < 0` test marks each opening corner as an inside corner of the plate. The reach check and `check_feature_spacing` use the rough offset of the selected thickness. The ISO object is reversed again after the seam, so the control reads a counter-clockwise opening that starts at the entry point.\n- **Mirrored entry (post).** The entry code moves to `crates/post/src/agie/contour/entry.rs`. For a die, the complete 2 mm hole must lie inside each wall. The chosen wall needs 3 mm of lead and 3 mm of straight wall on each side of the foot. The foot must clear each other wall by the swept margin (0.4 mm at 20 mm). A punch keeps the supporting exterior face rule.\n- **Text.** The refusals, the CPS description, the user guide and the `camcraft-mcp` skill row name the die opening. No new user-facing text uses the vendor name as a feature or post name (#3537).\n- **Example.** `examples/agie/die-plate.camscript` posts the `DIE20` job from an original 60 × 60 × 20 mm plate with a 38-sided opening.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Earlier offline control run (comment of 2026-11-20, old writer): Agie Control plotted all 38 faces at the inward offsets 0.245, 0.155, 0.140 and 0.134 mm. It cut the main profile and a 1.000 mm rough separation at X−12.255, then made three full trims. The threading point stayed at X−5.5 Y0. FORMALCHECK reported zero job errors. These offsets are the 20 mm row of `QN2_OFFSETS_UM`.\n- This port (CLI, `die-plate.camscript`): 41 moves, no warning, 760.19 mm² of captured waste. `DIE20.ISO` starts at `G00 X-12.50000 Y0.00000`, then `G01 X-12.50000 Y-6.00000` (counter-clockwise). `DIE20.SBL` is byte-identical to the control-checked `CCSEP20.SBL`, except the stem, the stock (70 × 70 mm at X−35 Y−35), the start hole (X−5.5 Y0) and `ID_PUNCH,c_die`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-post` `agie_safe_setup`: `die_setup_is_the_zero_step_punch_setup_with_the_die_side` (golden `crates/post/tests/golden/agie-setup/DIE20.SBL`), `die_setup_is_refused_on_every_thickness_but_20_mm`.\n- `camcraft-post` lib `agie::die_tests`: `a_die_enters_the_nearest_wall_from_inside_and_keeps_counter_clockwise_iso`, `a_die_hole_too_close_to_one_wall_enters_the_opposite_wall`, `a_die_hole_must_lie_completely_inside_the_opening`, `the_same_ring_with_an_inside_hole_is_refused_as_a_punch`, `the_reach_check_flips_every_opening_corner_to_an_inside_corner`, `a_reentrant_die_opening_is_refused`, `a_die_needs_the_rough_pass_and_wire_margin_to_the_stock`, `a_die_requires_the_qualified_20_mm_plate`, `a_die_publishes_the_zero_step_setup_with_the_die_side`.\n- `camcraft-app` `agie_native` (`die` module, the ported PR tests): `the_selected_die_rim_posts_nominal_walls_and_inward_compensation` (compares the CLI SBL with the `DIE20.SBL` golden), `an_outer_rim_an_external_pierce_or_an_incomplete_rim_cannot_publish_a_die`, `a_blind_floor_under_the_selected_upper_rim_cannot_publish_a_die`.\n- All #2955, #2964 and #2968 tests stay green without changes to their assertions.\n\n## Gate (head `d3443eddc`)\n\nHead `d3443eddc` merges the #2968 head `6443d4f09` into `30e6c4c3f`. That head contains `main` at `44e6a8269` (#3219). No rebase and no force-push.\n\nConflicts and resolution:\n- `crates/post/src/agie_setup.rs`: no conflict in this merge. The #2964 merge already resolved it: the `inspection` and `publish` modules of `main` come first, then `QN2_OFFSETS_UM`. `encode_die` and `ID_PUNCH,c_die` stay unchanged.\n- `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`, the Wire Contour row: the die text of this PR and the reentrant text of #2968 are both kept.\n- `docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md`, steps 3 and 4 of the control check: step 3 uses the row of the selected stock thickness (from #2964) and says that a die plate uses the 20 mm row. Step 4 keeps the die text of this PR. Step 1 says that a die is 20 mm only. The die corner text names the 20 mm row for the 0.245 mm offset.\n\nResults:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: batch plan, 1189 steps in 33.7 min, 1 failed, 0 stalled.\n  - The red step is `app suites: rotary_verify`, `a_rough_over_an_oversized_bar_peels_from_the_stock_radius` (2110 against 2064). This is the known red of `main` at `44e6a8269` (#3774, follow-up #3794). This PR does not change rotary code.\n  - Green: `clippy -D warnings`, `post suites: agie_inspection` (2), `agie_safe_setup` (8), `script_agie_native` (11), `app suites: agie_native` (16), `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Posted bytes: no file under `crates/post/tests/golden/agie-setup/` (`CCSEP20.SBL`, `DIE20.SBL`) changed against `30e6c4c3f`. `agie_safe_setup` and `agie_native` pass.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree d3443eddc origin/main` (`940cc5d0e`): clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The offline control import of the zero-step `DIE20` job ran on 2026-11-23 from head `30e6c4c3f`: see [the DIE20 control result](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2969#issuecomment-7115465528). It reported zero steps at import, the c_die side, inward offsets, the 1 mm separation, three trims and no FORMALCHECK error after TECCUT. The merge of `d3443eddc` does not change a posted byte. The control is an emulation, not the installed machine.\n- No physical cut was made.\n- Die thicknesses other than 20 mm and non-convex openings are refused. They have no control data.\n- Heavy lanes were not run (P6).\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: The native wire EDM job files post accepts a selected convex through-opening in a 20 mm plate. It writes the zero-step setup with the die side and checks the retained plate, the inward lead and the rough offset before it writes the job.\n\nFixes #2957\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
